<div class="wrap">
  <h1>Normain — Commit Review</h1>
  <div class="sub">2025-06-10 → 2026-06-10 · per-commit complexity / effort / thought ratings (1–10) + estimated human-hours · rated by 13 parallel Sonnet agents</div>

  <div class="kpis" id="kpis"></div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Output per month</h2>
    <p class="desc">Commit count (bars) vs estimated human-hours (line) — volume and weight don't always move together.</p>
    <div class="chart-box tall"><canvas id="cMonthly"></canvas></div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Average ratings per month</h2>
    <p class="desc">Complexity, effort, and thought (1–10). The step up from 2025-09 onward marks heavier work per commit.</p>
    <div class="chart-box"><canvas id="cRatings"></canvas></div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Rating distributions</h2>
      <p class="desc">How all 1,729 commits spread across the 1–10 scale.</p>
      <div class="chart-box"><canvas id="cDist"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Hours per commit</h2>
      <p class="desc">Most commits are small; a long tail carries the bulk of the hours.</p>
      <div class="chart-box"><canvas id="cHours"></canvas></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Commit types</h2>
      <p class="desc">Classified by leading subject keyword (repo doesn't use strict conventional commits).</p>
      <div class="chart-box"><canvas id="cTypes"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Cumulative estimated hours</h2>
      <p class="desc">Running total across the year.</p>
      <div class="chart-box"><canvas id="cCum"></canvas></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Heaviest commits</h2>
    <p class="desc">Top 15 by estimated hours.</p>
    <table id="tTop">
      <thead><tr><th>Hash</th><th>Date</th><th>Subject</th><th class="num">Cx</th><th class="num">Eff</th><th class="num">Th</th><th class="num">Hrs</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody></tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note">Method: each month was rated independently by a Sonnet sub-agent from commit subjects and diff stats (the ~10 largest commits per month inspected in depth). Ratings are directional, not ground truth; independent raters may drift in scale between months — part of the late-2025 step-up could be rubric drift. Month bucketing uses author date; totals match <code>git rev-list --count</code> exactly (1,729).</p>
</div>

